COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[311,"§Maryam\ndeeds\nEnsure, today, that you say only what pleases Allah, and remember this verse\nSay, \"I seek refuge with Allah from the accursed satan\", as satan incites to evil, but whoever seeks refuge with Allah, Allah will protect him.\nAsk Allah to gather you with the righteous.\nguid\nWhoever worships anything other than Allah, the worshiped will be his enemy on the Day of Resurrection.\nThe disbelievers and hypocrites hasten to commit evil, corruption and follow their lusts because devils entice and push them to do that.\nWhen it comes to your worship, do not pander to anyone, whether he is close or otherwise, because you will come alone on the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nوَنَرِثُهُۥ مَا يَقُولُ وَيَأۡتِينَا فَرۡدٗا ٨٠\nMeaning: We will take away the wealth and children that We have given him in this worldly life. Ibn Abbas (k) said: \"It means that We will inherit his wealth and children after We destroy him.\" Moreover, it is said: \"We will deprive him of what he wished for in the Hereafter, and give them to Muslims.\" (And he will come to Us alone), only himself, with no wealth, children or a tribe to help him. Al-Qurtubi: 13/509.\nUsing these verses, how do you advise one who is deluded by his wealth, authority, and children?\nوَنَرِثُهُۥ مَا يَقُولُ وَيَأۡتِينَا فَرۡدٗا ٨٠\nThis verse was revealed about one of the polytheists, Al-'As bin Wael Al-Sahmy, when he claimed that he would be given wealth and children in the Hereafter. Inheriting his children means that they would become Muslims, and they did. Amr bin Al-'as, the Companion, and Hisham bin Al-'as, the Companion who was martyred in the Battle of Ajnadayn. This was a glad tidings to the Prophet (ﷺ) and vexation and enragement of Al-'as bin Wael. Ibn Ashur: 16/163.\nIn this verse, what is the meaning of inheriting the children of Al-'As bin Wael Al-Sahmy?\nوَٱتَّخَذُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ ءَالِهَةٗ لِّيَكُونُواْ لَهُمۡ عِزّٗا ٨١ كَلَّاۚ سَيَكۡفُرُونَ بِعِبَادَتِهِمۡ وَيَكُونُونَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ضِدًّا ٨٢\nIf a servant relies on other than Allah, and attaches his hopes to that, he will be doomed; and if he seeks help from other than Allah, he will be forsaken. Ibn Taimyah: 4/292.\nThis verse indicates that If a servant relies on other than Allah and attaches his hopes to that, he will be doomed. How?\nيَوۡمَ نَحۡشُرُ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ إِلَى ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ وَفۡدٗا ٨٥\nThe righteous will come to the Most Merciful, hoping for His mercy and abundant grace, and hoping to attain His gifts in His Paradise, because of what they sent on ahead of good deeds, fearing Him and seeking His pleasure. Al-Saadi: 500.\nWhat will the righteous expect from their Lord when they are gathered to Him on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَنَسُوقُ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ وِرۡدٗا ٨٦\nThey will be driven toward Hellfire, thirsty - which is the worst state one may be in. They will be driven by way of humiliation and disgrace to the greatest prison and worst punishment, namely Hellfire, in a state of thirst and exhaustion. Al-Saadi: 500.\nThis verse depicts an awful picture for the polytheists on the Day of Resurrection. Explain.\nلَّا يَمۡلِكُونَ ٱلشَّفَٰعَةَ إِلَّا مَنِ ٱتَّخَذَ عِندَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ عَهۡدٗا ٨٧\nAllah describes belief in Him and following His Messengers as a covenant, because He has promised in His Books and on the lips of His Messengers an abundant reward for those who follow them. Al-Saadi: 501.\nAllah describes belief in Him and following His Messengers as a covenant. Why?\nتَكَادُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتُ يَتَفَطَّرۡنَ مِنۡهُ وَتَنشَقُّ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ وَتَخِرُّ ٱلۡجِبَالُ هَدًّا ٩٠ أَن دَعَوۡاْ لِلرَّحۡمَٰنِ وَلَدٗا ٩١\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"Verily, the heavens, the earth, the mountains and all creatures – except for humans and jinn – are frightened by the associating of partners with Allah.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/135.\nThe mountains and trees can be more sensible than some people. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nأَفَرَأَيتَHave you known?\nوَنَمُدُّ لَهُWe increase for him\nتَؤُزُّهُم أَزًّاConstantly inciting them to evil\nوِردًاWalking and thirsty\nيَتَفَطَّرنَThey rupture\nوَتَخِرُّ الجِبَالُ هَدًّاAnd the mountains collapse"],[312,"§Maryam, Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nRead Surat Maryam and extract two glad tidings and two warnings.\nShare a message in which you explain the easiest and shortest way, mentioned by this verse, to attain people's love.\nLearn Allah's Attributes, mentioned in Surat Ta-Ha, and invoke Him by them saying: \"O Most Merciful, have mercy on me; O Self-Sufficient, provide for me.\"\nguid\nPonder over past nations that were destroyed by Allah, do you hear any sound or sense any movement from them?\nLearning Arabic is a act of worship, as it helps to understand the Quran.\nRemember that Allah is fully aware of secrets and what is hidden, so do not say nor do anything that displeases Him.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ سَيَجۡعَلُ لَهُمُ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ وُدّٗا ٩٦\nMujahid said: \"Allah loves them and endears them to His believing servants.\" Harm bin Hayyan said: \"No servant who devotes himself to Allah except that Allah instills his love in the hearts of the believers and they love him.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/110.\nHow does the servant attain the love of Allah and His servants?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ سَيَجۡعَلُ لَهُمُ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ وُدّٗا ٩٦\n(Will endear them), Allah will make them beloved to His allies, and to the dwellers of heaven and earth, and, once people have love for them, many things will become easier for them and they will attain good things, people will pray for them, they will be guided, they will be well-accepted among people, and may attain positions of leadership. Al-Saadi: 501.\nFor a servant, what is the benefit of gaining the love of righteous people?\nفَإِنَّمَا يَسَّرۡنَٰهُ بِلِسَانِكَ لِتُبَشِّرَ بِهِ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ وَتُنذِرَ بِهِۦ قَوۡمٗا لُّدّٗا ٩٧\nMeaning: The Quran has been explained in your Arabic tongue, and became easy for those who ponder and reflect on it. Al-Qurtubi: 13/528.\nIs your endeavor to reflect on the Quran easy or difficult?\nمَآ أَنزَلۡنَا عَلَيۡكَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ لِتَشۡقَىٰٓ ٢ إِلَّا تَذۡكِرَةٗ لِّمَن يَخۡشَىٰ ٣\n(A reminder): Is the admonition that softens the hearts, leading them to comply to the command of Allah and avoid His prohibition. Those who fear Allah are singled out for mention because they benefit from it. Al-Shanqiti: 4/5.\nWhich trait enables you to benefit from reminding and admonishments?\nإِلَّا تَذۡكِرَةٗ لِّمَن يَخۡشَىٰ ٣\n(A reminder): Re-emergence of forgotten thoughts, for the Oneness of Allah is embedded in the mind. Human natural disposition inclines toward monotheism, while polytheism contradicts that. Thus, calling others to Islam serves as a reminder of what is in human natural disposition, or a reminder of the religion of Abraham (u). Ibn Ashur: 16/185.\nAllah says: (a reminder), instead of \"teaching\", why?\nوَإِن تَجۡهَرۡ بِٱلۡقَوۡلِ فَإِنَّهُۥ يَعۡلَمُ ٱلسِّرَّ وَأَخۡفَى ٧\nIbn Abbas (k) and Saeed bin Jubair said: \"A secret is what you keep in your heart, and what is more hidden is that which Allah prompts in your heart of things, which you are unaware that you speak to yourself about. Since you know what you keep in your heart today, but you do not know what you will keep tomorrow; however, Allah knows what you keep today and tomorrow.\" Ali bin Abi Talha narrated that Ibn Abbas (k) said: \"The secret is what a person keeps in his heart, and what is more hidden is what he will do in the future before doing it.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/113.\nExplain the greatness of Allah’s capability of knowing the secrets and what is more hidden.\nوَهَلۡ أَتَىٰكَ حَدِيثُ مُوسَىٰٓ ٩\nThe mention of Moses (u) story is a consolation to the Prophet (ﷺ) for facing hardships and disbelief from people. It set an example for him in carrying out his mission. Ibn Atiyah: 4/38.\nThe story of Moses (u) in Surat Ta-Ha induces tranquility and serenity. Reflect on it and draw two lessons from it.\nwords\nوُدًّاLove in His servants' hearts\nلُدًّاVery contentious in their falsehood\nقَرنٍA nation, generation\nرِكزًاA whisper, weak sound\nالثَّرَىWet soil, the seven earths beneath it\nبِقَبَسٍA torch for warmth"],[313,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nWrite down on a piece of paper the most important points in the story of Moses (u) that are helpful to a preacher in calling others to Allah.\nLook for a righteous and suitable friend for you, and work together in calling others to Allah.\nMake sure today to complete the daily remembrances of Allah in the morning and evening, after daily prayers, and before going to sleep.\nguid\nBeware of \"road bandits\" on your way to Allah.\nWorking to earn one's living and adopting the means is the way of the Prophets (p).\nBefore embarking on any work, the servant should ask for Allah's help and guidance.\nrefl\nإِنَّنِيٓ أَنَا ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنَا۠ فَٱعۡبُدۡنِي وَأَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ لِذِكۡرِيٓ ١٤\n(So worship Me): This refers to all kinds of worship, both visible and hidden, obligatory and supererogatory. Then He singles out prayer for mention - although it is included under the heading of worship - because of its virtue and high status, and because it is an act of worship that involves the heart, tongue, and physical faculties. Al-Saadi: 503.\nWhy is prayer mentioned even though it is included in worship?\nإِنَّنِيٓ أَنَا ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنَا۠ فَٱعۡبُدۡنِي وَأَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ لِذِكۡرِيٓ ١٤\nMeaning: So that you remember Me; , it is also said: so that I remember you. Ibn Juzay: 2/16.\nThis verse indicates an important aim for establishing prayer. What is it?\nوَمَا تِلۡكَ بِيَمِينِكَ يَٰمُوسَىٰ ١٧\nAllah asked Moses (u) about his staff only to show him his greatness in changing it into a snake; hence, the meaning of the question was to make Moses (u) confirm its existing condition, thus, he would realize the difference between its condition before and after it was turned into a snake. Ibn Juzay: 2/17.\nAllah asked Moses (u) about his staff even though He knows the secret and what is hidden. Why?\nٱذۡهَبۡ إِلَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِنَّهُۥ طَغَىٰ ٢٤ قَالَ رَبِّ ٱشۡرَحۡ لِي صَدۡرِي ٢٥ وَيَسِّرۡ لِيٓ أَمۡرِي ٢٦\nWhen Moses (u) received the command, he did not question it, despite his fear of Pharoh's transgression, rather, he asked for Allah's help in providing him with the means to deliver the message in an eloquent and convincing manner. Ibn Ashur: 16/210.\nExplain the Prophets' (p) promptness in submitting to and accepting Allah's command.\nرَبِّ ٱشۡرَحۡ لِي صَدۡرِي ٢٥\nMeaning: Expand and relax my chest so that I may bear with patience any offense in word and deed, and I would not be distressed by that or feel anxious. For if a person feels distressed and anxious, he will not be fit to call people for guidance. Al-Saadi: 504.\nThis verse encourages preachers to ask Allah to remove distress from them before engaging in calling others to Him. Explain\nقَالَ رَبِّ ٱشۡرَحۡ لِي صَدۡرِي ٢٥ وَيَسِّرۡ لِيٓ أَمۡرِي ٢٦\nMoses (u) asked Allah to widen his heart for the truth so that he would be certain that no one can harm him except with the permission of Allah. When he attained that knowledge, he would never fear Pharaoh with all of his tyranny, and numerous soldiers.Al-Baghawi: 3/119.\nWhen calling others to Allah, what was the way of the Prophets in tackling big concerns and intense obstacles?\nوَٱحۡلُلۡ عُقۡدَةٗ مِّن لِّسَانِي ٢٧ يَفۡقَهُواْ قَوۡلِي ٢٨\nThis refers to the lisp he had, which resulted from an incident when he was presented a date and a hot coal stone, and he placed the coal on his tongue instead of the date. However, he did not ask Allah to completely remove this affliction, rather, he asked for removal of his stammering, and people would understand the intended message in his speech. He was only asking for what was necessary to deliver his message. If he had asked for the removal of his affliction in its entirety, it would have been cured for him. However, the Prophets do not ask for anything more than what is needed. Ibn Kathir: 3/143.\nThe verse contains a Prophetic etiquette in invoking Allah for worldly needs. What is it?\nwords\nفَتَردَىYou would perish\nأَتَوَكَّأُ عَلَيهَاI lean upon it\nوَأَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلَى غَنَمِيI bring down leaves for my sheep\nمَآرِبُUses, needs\nسُوءٍLeprosy\nوَاحلُل عُقدَةًLoosen my tongue to be eloquent in speech\nاشدُد بِهِ أَزرِيStrengthen me with him"],[314,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to bestow upon you love from him and grant you acceptance as He does for His allies.\nEnjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, without fear.\nPursue a divine reward in attending a study circle with the intention of learning dialogue and debate, in order to use it for preaching to Allah.\nguid\nMoses and Aaron (q) were commanded not to slacken in remembering Allah on their way to meet Pharoh because Allah's remembrance eases things for people.\nIn calling others to Allah, a gentle speech is an effective argument and more likely to be accepted.\nThe allies of Allah are always in His care and protection.\nrefl\nوَأَلۡقَيۡتُ عَلَيۡكَ مَحَبَّةٗ مِّنِّي وَلِتُصۡنَعَ عَلَىٰ عَيۡنِيٓ ٣٩\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"Allah loved him and endeared him to His creation.\" Ibn Zaid said: \"It means: I made everyone who sees you loves you; until Pharaoh loved you and you were saved from his evil, and Asiya bint Muzahim loved you and adopted you as a son.\" Al-Qurtubi: 14/58.\nWho places the love for a servant in people's hearts?.\nوَٱصۡطَنَعۡتُكَ لِنَفۡسِي ٤١\nIf a lover wants to choose a beloved from among other people and cause him to reach a level of perfection that he could reach, he strives very hard and does all he can to help him reach that level. So what do you think about the Lord Who is Powerful and Most Generous, and what do you think He will do for the one whom He chose for Himself from among His creation? Al-Saadi: 506.\nThis verse indicates the virtue of Moses (u). How?\nٱذۡهَبۡ أَنتَ وَأَخُوكَ بِـَٔايَٰتِي وَلَا تَنِيَا فِي ذِكۡرِي ٤٢\nMeaning: Do not weaken in remembering Me for what I had enjoined and prohibited. Remembering Me will strengthen your resolve and make your feet firm, because by remembering Me you will remember My great favors and countless blessings. Al-Tabari: 18/312.\nWhat are the benefits that a preacher to Allah will gain from remembering Him?\nٱذۡهَبَآ إِلَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِنَّهُۥ طَغَىٰ ٤٣ فَقُولَا لَهُۥ قَوۡلٗا لَّيِّنٗا لَّعَلَّهُۥ يَتَذَكَّرُ أَوۡ يَخۡشَىٰ ٤٤\nYahya bin Mu'ath said about this verse: \"O Allah, this is Your forbearance with one who claimed to be a god, so how will Your forbearance be with one who says: You are the only God?\" Al-Qurtubi: 14/66.\nExplain an aspect of Allah's mercy toward His servants in light of this verse.\nفَقُولَا لَهُۥ قَوۡلٗا لَّيِّنٗا لَّعَلَّهُۥ يَتَذَكَّرُ أَوۡ يَخۡشَىٰ ٤٤\nThe objective of the mission of Allah's Messengers is guidance, not boasting and uttering harsh words to no avail. If leniency is not effective, and the one who is being called turns away and becomes arrogant, then it is permissible to use harsh words in admonishing him. Ibn Ashur: 16/225.\nCalling others to Allah requires wisdom. What does that mean?\nقَالَ فَمَن رَّبُّكُمَا يَٰمُوسَىٰ ٤٩\nPharaoh did not say: \"Who is my Lord?\", rather, he said: (Who is the Lord of you two), to avoid acknowledging the Lordship of Allah, even by repeating what they said, lest his followers and people would think he was unsure of knowing his Lord, or that he admitted that he had one. Ibn Ashur: 16/232.\nPharaoh did not say: \"Who is my Lord?\", but (Who is the Lord of you two). Why?\nقَالَ رَبُّنَا ٱلَّذِيٓ أَعۡطَىٰ كُلَّ شَيۡءٍ خَلۡقَهُۥ ثُمَّ هَدَىٰ ٥٠\nAlhasan and Qatadah said: \"Allah gave each thing what is best for it, and guided it to the best.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/124.\nExplain Allah's blessing upon his creation by giving and guiding them.\nwords\nاليَمِّThe Nile river\nيَكفُلُهُOne who can nurse him\nتَقَرَّ عَينُهَاShe may rejoice\nوَفَتَنَّاكَ فُتُونًاWe put you through several trials\nعَلَى قَدَرٍAt the decreed time\nوَلاَ تَنِيَاDo not slacken nor become weak\nيَفرُطَHe will hasten punishment against us"],[315,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nGive a talk or share a message about the risk of magic.\nCooperating with some of your collogues, offer advice to a magician, a fortune teller or to one who openly commits sins, remind him of the graveness of his sin and Allah's great forgiveness and mercy.\nForbid a wrong that you saw your collogues were doing.\nguid\nIt is permissible to engage in a debate to establish truth and nullify falsehood.\nDo not engage in a debate unless you have knowledge, insight and witnesses.\nPreachers and students of Islamic knowledge have greater reason to cooperate in delivering the message of Islam to others.\nrefl\nٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ مَهۡدٗا وَسَلَكَ لَكُمۡ فِيهَا سُبُلٗا وَأَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءٗ فَأَخۡرَجۡنَا بِهِۦٓ أَزۡوَٰجٗا مِّن نَّبَاتٖ شَتَّىٰ ٥٣\n(It is He Who spread out the earth for you), like a bed. Moreover, see how Moses (u) described his Lord with attributes that Pharaoh cannot attain, neither realistically nor metaphorically. Had Moses (u) described Allah as: \"the Creator\", “the Sustainer”, Pharaoh would have misconstrued that and claimed the same for himself. Ibn Juzay: 2/20.\nThe effective preacher should be convincing in his argument; how can you learn that from the dialogue between Moses (u) and Pharaoh?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّأُوْلِي ٱلنُّهَىٰ ٥٤\n(There are signs in this for people of sound intellect) to those who use reason. In the Arabic text, the word \"Nuha\" is used, which means a good judgment that keeps one from falling into sins and disgrace. Al-Baghawi: 3/126.\nAllah refers to the people who use reason as those who have (Nuha). Why?\nكُلُواْ وَٱرۡعَوۡاْ أَنۡعَٰمَكُمۡۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّأُوْلِي ٱلنُّهَىٰ ٥٤\nAllah singles out people of sound intellect here because they are the ones who benefit from the signs and reflect on them. As for others, they are more akin to grazing animals, for they do not look at the signs and reflect upon them, and they do not think deeply in order to find the purpose behind them. Rather, their share is that of animals that eat and drink whilst living a life of heedlessness, and turning away from the truth. Al-Saadi: 507.\nWho benefits from the outcomes of Allah's blessings and His power, and recognizes their aims?\nقَالَ أَجِئۡتَنَا لِتُخۡرِجَنَا مِنۡ أَرۡضِنَا بِسِحۡرِكَ يَٰمُوسَىٰ ٥٧\nPharaoh claimed that these signs that Moses (u) showed him were no more than magic and illusions, the purpose of which was to drive them from their land and take it over, so that his [Pharaoh's] words would have some impact on his people, for people are naturally inclined toward their homelands, and it is difficult for them to leave them. Al-Saadi: 508.\nPharaoh accused Moses (u) that he came to drive him and his people from their land. Why?\nقَالَ مَوۡعِدُكُمۡ يَوۡمُ ٱلزِّينَةِ وَأَن يُحۡشَرَ ٱلنَّاسُ ضُحٗى ٥٩ فَتَوَلَّىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنُ فَجَمَعَ كَيۡدَهُۥ ثُمَّ أَتَىٰ ٦٠\nMoses (u) appointed for them the day of the festival in order to raise high the word and religion of Allah and debase the disbelievers with their falsehood for all people to see in the crowded gathering, thus, strengthening the desire of those who search for the truth while weakening the falsifiers and their followers. Moreover, the news of this encounter would travel throughout the land by the spectators' talks and reach every house inside the community and outside. Al-Qurtubi: 14/86.\nMoses (u) appointed the day of the festival for Pharaoh and his people. Why?\nفَتَوَلَّىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنُ فَجَمَعَ كَيۡدَهُۥ ثُمَّ أَتَىٰ ٦٠\nThe phrase \"putting together\" refers to planning the encounter against Moses (u), setting up the tricks to show the superiority of the magicians over him, and convincing the attending crowd that Moses (u) has nothing to show for. This is an old style of debating in which one side tries to show the falsehood of his opponent's argument, using all means to confuse, culminate, and defame him. Moreover, startling him with things that weaken his resolve and bewilder his mind until he loses control. Ibn Ashur: 16/247.\nThe verse mentions one of Pharaoh's debating styles. What is it?\nفَأَجۡمِعُواْ كَيۡدَكُمۡ ثُمَّ ٱئۡتُواْ صَفّٗاۚ\nBecause that is more convenient for your performance, and will create greater awe in people's hearts, and so that none of you will do less than he is able to. Al-Saadi: 508.\nWhy did the magicians advised each other of coming forward in line?\nwords\nمَهدًاEasy and spread out to benefit you\nسُبُلًاPathways\nلِأُولِي النُّهَىThose of sound intellect\nسُوىًA level, even [place]\nيَومُ الزِّينَةِThe festival day\nفَيُسحِتَكُمHe will exterminate you\nبِطَرِيقَتِكُمُ المُثلَىYour most exemplary way [magic]"],[316,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you warn others against magic and magicians.\nSay, \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\"\nShare a message in which you give glad tidings that threats made by tyrants do not always come about, because the judgement belongs to Allah before and after.\nguid\nA sign of tyrants' foolishness is threatening the people of truth with power and punishment.\nWhen facing a hard trial, the preacher should compare it to what in store for him in the Hereafter, as this will make his hardship easy for him, and he will endure it patiently.\nThe harder the trial, the closer is the relief.\nrefl\nقَالُواْ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ إِمَّآ أَن تُلۡقِيَ وَإِمَّآ أَن نَّكُونَ أَوَّلَ مَنۡ أَلۡقَىٰ ٦٥ قَالَ بَلۡ أَلۡقُواْۖ فَإِذَا حِبَالُهُمۡ وَعِصِيُّهُمۡ يُخَيَّلُ إِلَيۡهِ مِن سِحۡرِهِمۡ أَنَّهَا تَسۡعَىٰ ٦٦\nThey gave him the choice to create the impression that they were confident they would prevail over him, regardless of the circumstances. Al-Saadi: 508.\nThe self-confidence of the people of falsehood does not unsettle the confidence of the believer in his Lord. Explain in view of this verse.\nفَأَوۡجَسَ فِي نَفۡسِهِۦ خِيفَةٗ مُّوسَىٰ ٦٧\nAs is human nature; otherwise, he was certain of the promise and support of Allah. Al-Saadi: 508.\nWhy did Moses (u) sense fear? Was he skeptical about Allah's promise?\nوَلَا يُفۡلِحُ ٱلسَّاحِرُ حَيۡثُ أَتَىٰ ٦٩\nA magician will never succeed in every aspect of his life, and this is confirmed by collectively mentioning all the places he may be in, as Allah says, (wherever he goes). This proves the infidelity of the magician since anyone who becomes completely deprived of prosperity has no good left in him and that is a disbeliever. Al-Shanqiti: 4/39.\nA magician will never succeed, why?\nقَالَ ءَامَنتُمۡ لَهُۥ قَبۡلَ أَنۡ ءَاذَنَ لَكُمۡۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَكَبِيرُكُمُ ٱلَّذِي عَلَّمَكُمُ ٱلسِّحۡرَۖ فَلَأُقَطِّعَنَّ أَيۡدِيَكُمۡ وَأَرۡجُلَكُم مِّنۡ خِلَٰفٖ وَلَأُصَلِّبَنَّكُمۡ فِي جُذُوعِ ٱلنَّخۡلِ وَلَتَعۡلَمُنَّ أَيُّنَآ أَشَدُّ عَذَابٗا وَأَبۡقَىٰ ٧١\nWhen Pharaoh saw the magicians' belief in Moses (u), he became enraged and wanted to punish them, but punishing them as a result of debating Moses (u) would be contradictory to what he agreed to set up the debate for. So, in order to get back at them, he considered their declaration of belief before taking his permission as a challenge to his authority. Ibn Ashur: 16/263.\nThe defeated usually makes up hollow excuses. Explain in view of this verse.\nقَالُواْ لَن نُّؤۡثِرَكَ عَلَىٰ مَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ ٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ وَٱلَّذِي فَطَرَنَاۖ فَٱقۡضِ مَآ أَنتَ قَاضٍۖ إِنَّمَا تَقۡضِي هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَآ ٧٢\nWhen they accepted the faith and were certain of it, they dismissed his threat and punishment. This is the situation of the followers of Messengers when they become enlightened by the lights of the Message, they would soon be transformed from the ignorance and rigidness of disbelief to the wisdom and firmness of faith. Ibn Ashur: 16/266.\nDescribe the situation of believers when they become enlightened by the lights of the Message.\nقَالُواْ لَن نُّؤۡثِرَكَ عَلَىٰ مَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ ٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ وَٱلَّذِي فَطَرَنَاۖ فَٱقۡضِ مَآ أَنتَ قَاضٍۖ إِنَّمَا تَقۡضِي هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَآ ٧٢\nThese words of the magicians indicate that a wise person should weigh up between the pleasures of this world and the pleasures of the Hereafter, and between punishment in this world and punishment in the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 509.\nIf you are faced with a prohibited lustful desire, this verse shows you a way out. Explain.\nإِنَّهُۥ مَن يَأۡتِ رَبَّهُۥ مُجۡرِمٗا فَإِنَّ لَهُۥ جَهَنَّمَ لَا يَمُوتُ فِيهَا وَلَا يَحۡيَىٰ ٧٤\nTherefore, he does not benefit from living nor is he relieved by death. Moreover, it is said that the disbeliever's soul will be hanging in his throat, as describes by Allah, thus, he does not die if it moves, nor does he live if it remains. Al-Qurtubi: 14/107.\nExplain the intensity of Allah's punishment for the disbeliever as being between life and death.\nwords\nفَأَوجَسَHe sensed within himself\nتَلقَفIt swallows up\nمِن خِلاَفٍOn opposite sides\nلن نُؤثِرَكَWe will not favor you\nفَطَرَنَاHe who created us\nفَاقضِDecree, decide"],[317,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nSay, \"O my Lord, Praise be to You, for You saved me from that tribulation; You protected me from that trial, and You relieved me from the adversity of such and such.\"\nSeek refuge with Allah from the causes of His wrath.\nMention Allah's Name before eating, thank Him afterward and avoid exceeding the limits and showing off.\nguid\nBe certain of Allah's promise, and do not fear falsehood or its people.\nExceeding the limits, transgressing and being ungrateful are all prohibited.\nAmong the traits of the Prophets (p) is feeling grief and sorrow when a sin is committed or an act of obedience is neglected.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ أَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنۡ أَسۡرِ بِعِبَادِي فَٱضۡرِبۡ لَهُمۡ طَرِيقٗا فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ يَبَسٗا لَّا تَخَٰفُ دَرَكٗا وَلَا تَخۡشَىٰ ٧٧\nAllah's promise of not being overtaken was directed to Moses (u) only since he was the example for his people; hence if he did not show any fear, then they would have courage and their faith would be strengthened. Ibn Ashur: 16/270.\nAllah's promise of not being overtaken was directed to Moses (u) only. Why?\nوَلَا تَطۡغَوۡاْ فِيهِ فَيَحِلَّ عَلَيۡكُمۡ غَضَبِيۖ وَمَن يَحۡلِلۡ عَلَيۡهِ غَضَبِي فَقَدۡ هَوَىٰ ٨١\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"Do not transgress.\" Al-Kalbi said: \"Do not be ungrateful for the blessings lest you become transgressors and tyrants.\" It is also said: \"Do not spend your wealth in My disobedience.\" Moreover, it is said: \"Do not use My blessing to disobey Me.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/134.\nWhen does a servant reach the limit of excessiveness for which punishment will occur?\nوَإِنِّي لَغَفَّارٞ لِّمَن تَابَ وَءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗا ثُمَّ ٱهۡتَدَىٰ ٨٢\nIndeed, all measures [of repentance] are limited to these things, for repentance erases what came before it, faith and Islam cancel out what came before, and righteous deeds erase bad deeds. Being steadfast in following the path of guidance in all ways, such as acquiring knowledge and reflecting upon a verse or hadith, so that one may understand the meaning that will help him to be steadfast and call others to the true religion, and refute innovation or disbelief or misguidance, as well as Jihad, migration and other aspects of steadfastness in Islam, all expiate sins and fulfill the purpose. Al-Saadi: 511.\nThe verse mentions three causes for forgiveness. What are they?\nوَمَآ أَعۡجَلَكَ عَن قَوۡمِكَ يَٰمُوسَىٰ ٨٣\nWhen Moses (u) was commanded to proceed with the Children of Israel to Mount Tur, he hastened by himself seeking to please Allah, and asked the Children of Israel to follow behind. He appointed his brother Aaron in charge of them, and that when the Samiri ordered them to worship the calf. Ibn Juzay: 2/23.\nWhat made Moses (u) hasten?\nوَعَجِلۡتُ إِلَيۡكَ رَبِّ لِتَرۡضَىٰ ٨٤\nMeaning: I hastened to the place to which You commanded me to go so that You would be pleased with me. Al-Qurtubi: 14/117.\nWhich trait of the worshiper that increases Allah's pleasure? .\nفَرَجَعَ مُوسَىٰٓ إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦ غَضۡبَٰنَ أَسِفٗاۚ\nMeaning: After Allah informed him of what they were doing, he became extremely angry and upset with them. He was very worried for them. During this time, he received the Torah, which contained their Sharia (Law), this was a great honor for them, for they were a people who used to worship other than Allah. Ibn Kathir: 3/157.\nProphets and preachers are among the most compassionate toward the Muslim nation. Explain in view of this verse.\nقَالُواْ مَآ أَخۡلَفۡنَا مَوۡعِدَكَ بِمَلۡكِنَا وَلَٰكِنَّا حُمِّلۡنَآ أَوۡزَارٗا مِّن زِينَةِ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ فَقَذَفۡنَٰهَا فَكَذَٰلِكَ أَلۡقَى ٱلسَّامِرِيُّ ٨٧\nThe summary of their apology was that these ignorant people refrained from taking the ornaments of the Copts, and they threw them out, but worshiped a calf in the process. So, they refrained from doing a trifling matter and perpetrated the biggest sin. Al-Shanqiti: 4/87.\nIn view of this verse, explain the harm of refrainment that is based on ignorance.\nwords\nأَسرِTravel by night\nدَرَكًاBeing overtaken\nالمَنَّFood; like honey\nوَالسَّلوَىA bird, like quail\nعَلَى أَثَرِيThey are close upon my tracks\nبِمَلكِنَاBy our own choice and will\nمِن زِينَةِ القَومِFrom the ornaments of the people of Pharaoh"],[318,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nForbid a wrong, with your words or heart if you could not change it by hand.\nLet your beard grow, and do not shave it since it is the Sunnah of the Prophets (p).\nSeek refuge with Allah from the soul that is persistent enjoiner of evil, which makes committing a sin appealing.\nguid\nReproaching among brothers does not sever the ties of brotherhood.\nUsing a gentle response in dealing with an angry person, and calling him with what softens his heart is the best way to calm his anger.\nRemoving falsehood from people's hearts must be done wisely in order to convince them of its nullity.\nrefl\nأَفَلَا يَرَوۡنَ أَلَّا يَرۡجِعُ إِلَيۡهِمۡ قَوۡلٗا وَلَا يَمۡلِكُ لَهُمۡ ضَرّٗا وَلَا نَفۡعٗا ٨٩\nIn this verse, the mention of power to harm precedes the power to benefit in order to leave no excuse for them to consider it divine, for the excuse of one fearing harm is more powerful than that of one seeking benefit. Ibn Ashur: 16/289.\nIn this verse, the mention of power to harm precedes the power to benefit. Why?\nأَفَلَا يَرَوۡنَ أَلَّا يَرۡجِعُ إِلَيۡهِمۡ قَوۡلٗا وَلَا يَمۡلِكُ لَهُمۡ ضَرّٗا وَلَا نَفۡعٗا ٨٩\nThe lesson here is that this idol lacks the attributes of the sane because when they call on it, praise and glorify it, it remains silent, does not appreciate nor promise to answer their calls. The attribute of one who is perfect is that when he hears a praise or receive a request, he answers back. Ibn Ashur: 16/288.\nAmong the proofs of falsehood of worshiping idols, shrines and gravesites is that they do not respond to their worshipers. How does the verse indicate this fact?\nقَالَ يَٰهَٰرُونُ مَا مَنَعَكَ إِذۡ رَأَيۡتَهُمۡ ضَلُّوٓاْ ٩٢ أَلَّا تَتَّبِعَنِۖ أَفَعَصَيۡتَ أَمۡرِي ٩٣\nThis is a fundamental principle in enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong. It is obligated to change the wrong and boycott its perpetrators, and that whoever stays with them, specially if he is content with their action, is subject to the same ruling as they are. Al-Qurtubi: 14/124.\nThis verse contains a fundamental principle from which every believer benefits. What is it?\nقَالَ يَبۡنَؤُمَّ لَا تَأۡخُذۡ بِلِحۡيَتِي وَلَا بِرَأۡسِيٓۖ\nEven though Aaron was Moses' full brother, his mentioning of the mother was Aaron's attempt to soften Moses' anger. The mentioning of the mother here is more delicate and profound in bringing about gentleness and mildness. Ibn Kathir: 3/159.\nAaron called Moses: (O son of my mother), even though he was Moses' full brother. Why?\nقَالَ يَبۡنَؤُمَّ لَا تَأۡخُذۡ بِلِحۡيَتِي وَلَا بِرَأۡسِيٓۖ\nThis verse in tandem with another in Surat Al-An'am prove that growing a beard is mandatory. It is Quranic evidence to grow the beard and not shave it. The verse in Surat Al-An'am is: (And among his descendants: David, Solomon, Job, Joseph, Moses, and Aaron), then after listing these honorable Prophets, Allah says, (they are those whom Allah has guided, so follow their guidance) [6:90]. This proves that Aaron is among the Prophets of whom our Prophet (ﷺ) was commanded to follow. A command to the Prophet (ﷺ) is also a command to his followers. Al-Shanqiti: 4/92.\nHow do we infer from this verse a proof for growing a beard?\nقَالَ فَٱذۡهَبۡ فَإِنَّ لَكَ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ أَن تَقُولَ لَا مِسَاسَۖ وَإِنَّ لَكَ مَوۡعِدٗا لَّن تُخۡلَفَهُۥۖ\nThis verse presents a fundamental principal in dealing with innovators and sinners through expulsion, abandonment, and boycott. The Prophet (ﷺ) did that with Ka'b bin Malik who was among the three (j) who stayed behind during the battle of Tabuk. Al-Qurtubi: 14/130.\nIn view of this verse, how should we deal with many of those who call to religious innovation and misguidance at the present time?\nوَٱنظُرۡ إِلَىٰٓ إِلَٰهِكَ ٱلَّذِي ظَلۡتَ عَلَيۡهِ عَاكِفٗاۖ لَّنُحَرِّقَنَّهُۥ ثُمَّ لَنَنسِفَنَّهُۥ فِي ٱلۡيَمِّ نَسۡفًا ٩٧\nMoses (u) did that, and if it had been a god it would have protected itself from the one who intended to harm it and wanted to destroy it. The hearts of the Israelites had been filled with love for the calf, so Moses (u) wanted to destroy it as they were looking on, in such a way that it could not be restored, by burning it, crushing it and scattering its remains in the sea, so as to remove love for it from their hearts, just as the thing itself was to be removed. Al-Saadi: 512.\nWhy did Moses (u) destroy the calf the way he did?\nwords\nجَسَدًاA statue of gold\nلَهُ خُوَارٌHas a mooing sound\nلَن نَبرَحَWe will never cease\nوَلَم تَرقُب قَولِيYou did not observe my words of looking after them\nبَصُرتُI saw or had an insight\nلاَ مِسَاسَAn outcast; saying to every one: I will not touch you nor will you touch me"],[319,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nRead one of the stories of past nations to benefit from its lessons and admonitions.\nRead a Surah from the Quran while reflecting on its general subject.\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You for the intercession of the Prophet (ﷺ) on the Day of Resurrection.\"\nguid\nApproach the Holy Quran through learning, teaching, and practicing, for it is the salvation for mankind.\nThink about the day when all voices will be stilled before Allah, so that only whisper will be heard due to the enormity of the terror in which they will be.\nRemember that intercession will not benefit one unless Allah permits the intercessor, and is pleased with the one who is interceded for.\nrefl\nكَذَٰلِكَ نَقُصُّ عَلَيۡكَ مِنۡ أَنۢبَآءِ مَا قَدۡ سَبَقَۚ وَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَٰكَ مِن لَّدُنَّا ذِكۡرٗا ٩٩\nWhat has been narrated about past nations is not intended for a pastime, or entertaining the listeners, rather, it is intended to admonish, remind, and awaken the consciences of Arab polytheists to heed the lesson from this narration. Ibn Ashur: 16/302.\nWhat is the intention of narrating the stories of past nations in the Quran?\nوَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَٰكَ مِن لَّدُنَّا ذِكۡرٗا ٩٩\nNamely this Holy Quran, which is a reminder of narrations of the past and future, and a reminder that makes one reflect on what Allah possesses of perfect names and attributes, through which one may be reminded of rulings, commands, prohibitions and requital. Al-Saadi: 512.\nWhy is the Quran called a (Reminder)?\nيَتَخَٰفَتُونَ بَيۡنَهُمۡ إِن لَّبِثۡتُمۡ إِلَّا عَشۡرٗا ١٠٣ نَّحۡنُ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا يَقُولُونَ إِذۡ يَقُولُ أَمۡثَلُهُمۡ طَرِيقَةً إِن لَّبِثۡتُمۡ إِلَّا يَوۡمٗا ١٠٤\nMeaning: Some will say to others privately: \"You only stayed ten nights in worldly life.\" They will say that because they belittle the timespan of this world. It is also said that they mean the time they spent in their graves. (The most discerning among them will say, \"You stayed no more than a day\"), the most knowledgeable among them will say: \"You stayed for one day only,\" thus, he belittles the time even more than they did. Ibn Juzay: 2/24.\nHow does this verse indicate the insignificance of this worldly life?\nيَتَخَٰفَتُونَ بَيۡنَهُمۡ إِن لَّبِثۡتُمۡ إِلَّا عَشۡرٗا ١٠٣ نَّحۡنُ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا يَقُولُونَ إِذۡ يَقُولُ أَمۡثَلُهُمۡ طَرِيقَةً إِن لَّبِثۡتُمۡ إِلَّا يَوۡمٗا ١٠٤\nWhat this signifies is great regret at how they wasted that short time and spent it careless and negligent, turning away from that which would have benefitted them and turning towards that which harmed them, and now requital has come and the warning of punishment will inevitably be fulfilled. So, there is nothing left but regret and calls for doom and destruction. Al-Saadi: 513.\nWhat benefit does one gain from learning about the criminals in this situation?\nوَعَنَتِ ٱلۡوُجُوهُ لِلۡحَيِّ ٱلۡقَيُّومِۖ وَقَدۡ خَابَ مَنۡ حَمَلَ ظُلۡمٗا ١١١\nThe word (faces) is used to represent people since the effects of humility appear on the face. Al-Qurtubi: 14/142.\nThe word (faces) is used in this verse to represent people. Why?\nوَمَن يَعۡمَلۡ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَهُوَ مُؤۡمِنٞ فَلَا يَخَافُ ظُلۡمٗا وَلَا هَضۡمٗا ١١٢\n(While he is a believer), since no deed will be accepted without belief. Al-Qurtubi: 14/143.\nExplain the importance of belief for accepting righteous deeds.\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ قُرۡءَانًا عَرَبِيّٗا وَصَرَّفۡنَا فِيهِ مِنَ ٱلۡوَعِيدِ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَّقُونَ أَوۡ يُحۡدِثُ لَهُمۡ ذِكۡرٗا ١١٣\nThis description implies praise for the Quran because the Arabic language is the most eloquent and expressive among all languages. Ibn Ashur: 16/314.\nWhat does describing the Quran as (an Arabic) indicate?\nwords\nزُرقًاThey will be blue-eyed with blackened faces\nيَتَخَافَتُونَThey whisper\nأَمثَلُهُمThe most discerning among them\nقَاعًاA bare land with no vegetation\nصَفصَفًاA leveled land\nوَلاَ أَمتًاAn elevation\nوَعَنَتِThey are humbled\nهَضمًاA curtailment of his reward"],[320,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nAsk Allah often to increasing your knowledge.\nSeek refuge with Allah for yourself, your wife and children from the accursed satan.\nRecall a sin that you had committed and seek Allah's forgiveness persistently so that He may choose you.\nguid\nAmong the weaknesses of children of Adam through which Iblis can infiltrate are discontent with provision and wishing for a long life.\nEnsure that you know the background of one who offers you advice before accepting his advice.\nAdhering to the Quran is a cause for joy in this life and the Hereafter while turning away from it is a cause for misery in this life and the Hereafter.\nrefl\nفَتَعَٰلَى ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمَلِكُ ٱلۡحَقُّۗ\nIn describing His Sovereignty as (The True), Allah points to the fact that the sovereignty of other worldly kings is flawed. Ibn Ashur: 16/315.\nIn brief, list three differences between the Sovereignty of Allah and that of worldly kings.\nوَلَا تَعۡجَلۡ بِٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ مِن قَبۡلِ أَن يُقۡضَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكَ وَحۡيُهُۥۖ وَقُل رَّبِّ زِدۡنِي عِلۡمٗا ١١٤\nFrom this verse we learn the etiquette of receiving knowledge, and that the one who listens to knowledge must be patient and wait until the teacher has finished speaking, because what he wants to say is interconnected. Then when he has finished, the one who has questions may ask him. He should not hasten to ask questions and interrupt the teacher when he is speaking, because that is a cause of being deprived of knowledge. Al-Saadi: 514.\nWhat etiquette should a student of Islamic knowledge learn from this verse?\nوَلَا تَعۡجَلۡ بِٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ مِن قَبۡلِ أَن يُقۡضَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكَ وَحۡيُهُۥۖ وَقُل رَّبِّ زِدۡنِي عِلۡمٗا ١١٤\nSince the Prophet's (ﷺ) hastening to repeat the Revelation was indicative of his perfect love for knowledge and his eagerness to acquire it, Allah instructed him to ask Him to increase his knowledge. Al-Saadi: 514.\nThis verse indicates an important means to acquire knowledge. What is it?\nوَقُل رَّبِّ زِدۡنِي عِلۡمٗا ١١٤\nWhenever Abdullah bin Masoud (t) read this verse, he used to say: \"O Allah, increase my knowledge, faith, and conviction.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/142.\nHow should we reflect on this verse and adhere to it?\nإِنَّ لَكَ أَلَّا تَجُوعَ فِيهَا وَلَا تَعۡرَىٰ ١١٨ وَأَنَّكَ لَا تَظۡمَؤُاْ فِيهَا وَلَا تَضۡحَىٰ ١١٩\nAllah links between the absence of hunger and clothing in saying: (you will neither go hungry nor naked), because of the parallel between hunger and bareness in that hunger is the lack of protection of the inside from pain, which is food, and bareness is the lack of protection of the outside from the elements, which is clothes. Allah links between the absence of thirst and pain from the sun's heat in saying: (nor will you suffer from thirst or from scorching heat), because of the parallel between thirst and the sun's heat in that thirst causes pain within the body, and the sun's heat causes pain to the outside of the body. Ibn Ashur: 16/322.\nIn this verse, hunger and bareness are linked together, and thirst and pain from the sun's heat are linked together. Why?\nفَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَ هُدَايَ فَلَا يَضِلُّ وَلَا يَشۡقَىٰ ١٢٣\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"Allah pledged that whoever reads the Quran and follows its teachings, will not go astray in this life nor will he fall into misery in the Hereafter,\" then, he recited this verse. Al-Qurtubi: 14/156.\nIs memorizing the Quran enough for guidance in this life and salvation in the Hereafter?\nوَمَنۡ أَعۡرَضَ عَن ذِكۡرِي فَإِنَّ لَهُۥ مَعِيشَةٗ ضَنكٗا\nMeaning: His life will be hard in this world, and he will have no tranquility nor comfort in his chest. Rather, his chest will be constrained and in difficulty due to his misguidance. Even if he appears to be in comfort outwardly, wears whatever he wants, eats whatever he likes, and lives wherever he wants, he will not be happy. If his heart does not have pure certainty and guidance, he will be in agitation, bewilderment and doubt, and will always be in confusion and a state of uncertainty. This what miserable life is. Ibn Kathir: 3/164.\nIs the outward pleasure a sign of true happiness? Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nفَتَعَالَىExalted and high is Allah\nعَزمًاCarrying out what he was commanded\nوَطَفِقَاThey began\nيَخصِفَانِThey put together\nاجتَبَاهُHe chose him\nضَنكًاA miserable, difficult"],[321,"§Ta-Ha\ndeeds\nKeep a regular session to review your memorized portion of the Quran, and do not forget it.\nSay the morning Athkar before sunrise and the evening Athkar before sunset, and do not forget to glorify Allah during the rest of the day and night.\nEnjoin your brethren and household to perform prayer on time.\nguid\nA preacher should follow the example of the Prophet (ﷺ) in his patience against the abuse of those whom he called to Allah.\nIf you are subjected to any kind of abuse, ensure to glorify Allah often, specially after Al-Fajr and Al-Maghrib prayers, for it is a comfort to the heart.\nWhen you see someone whom Allah has given more than you of worldly gains , do not aspire to what he has, and remember that Allah has given you more than him of religious knowledge and deeds.\nrefl\nقَالَ كَذَٰلِكَ أَتَتۡكَ ءَايَٰتُنَا فَنَسِيتَهَاۖ وَكَذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ تُنسَىٰ ١٢٦\nIn this verse, forgetfulness means abandonment. (You will be forgotten) abandoned in punishment. Ibn Atiyah: 4/69.\nWhat is meant by forgetfulness in this verse?\nوَلَعَذَابُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ أَشَدُّ وَأَبۡقَىٰٓ ١٢٧\nBecause it never ends, unlike worldly punishment, which does come to an end. So, what is required is to fear Allah and beware of the punishment of the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 516.\nA Muslim may face hardships in his life, how can he learn from this verse to alleviate these hardships?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ عَلَىٰ مَا يَقُولُونَ وَسَبِّحۡ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّكَ قَبۡلَ طُلُوعِ ٱلشَّمۡسِ وَقَبۡلَ غُرُوبِهَاۖ وَمِنۡ ءَانَآيِٕ ٱلَّيۡلِ فَسَبِّحۡ وَأَطۡرَافَ ٱلنَّهَارِ لَعَلَّكَ تَرۡضَىٰ ١٣٠\nAllah commanded His Prophet (ﷺ) to continue to purify himself and his family with prayer, and turn away from worldly adornments that Allah Had given to the disbelievers; and He promised him that the best outcome is for the righteous. Ibn Ashur: 16/337.\nWhen the abuse of the polytheists increases, the Muslim should turn to purifying and strengthening himself through worshiping in order to stand firm against their abuse. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيۡنَيۡكَ إِلَىٰ مَا مَتَّعۡنَا بِهِۦٓ أَزۡوَٰجٗا مِّنۡهُمۡ زَهۡرَةَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا لِنَفۡتِنَهُمۡ فِيهِۚ وَرِزۡقُ رَبِّكَ خَيۡرٞ وَأَبۡقَىٰ ١٣١\nThis verse indicates that if an individual notices in himself any aspiration for the adornment of this world and finds himself interested in pursuing it, he should remind himself of what lies ahead in the Hereafter of the provision of his Lord, and he should weigh up the two matters. Al-Saadi: 517.\nA Muslim, sometimes, aspires to be among those who are enjoying the pleasures of this worldly life. How should he deal with that feeling?\nوَأۡمُرۡ أَهۡلَكَ بِٱلصَّلَوٰةِ وَٱصۡطَبِرۡ عَلَيۡهَاۖ\nEnjoining prayer also implicitly enjoins everything without which it cannot be completed. Hence, this is a command to teach them how to pray, teach them what could invalidate the prayer, and teach them how to pray properly. If the servant performs his prayer in the manner enjoined, he will be more careful and observant with regard to other matters of his religion, but if he neglects it, he will be more careless with regard to other matters. Al-Saadi: 517.\nEnjoining the family to perform prayer, how should that be done? Among all acts of worship, why is prayer singled out for enjoining and being steadfast therein?\nوَأۡمُرۡ أَهۡلَكَ بِٱلصَّلَوٰةِ وَٱصۡطَبِرۡ عَلَيۡهَاۖ لَا نَسۡـَٔلُكَ رِزۡقٗاۖ نَّحۡنُ نَرۡزُقُكَۗ وَٱلۡعَٰقِبَةُ لِلتَّقۡوَىٰ ١٣٢\n(We ask no provision from you), We do not ask you to provide provision for your and your family, so you and your family dedicate yourselves for prayer because We will give you provision. When one of righteous predecessors lacked provision for his family, he used to say to them: \"Get up and pray, as Allah commanded you as such,\" then he recited this verse. Ibn Juzay: 2/29.\nThis verse contains a great bounty and one of the benefits of prayer. What is it?\nوَأۡمُرۡ أَهۡلَكَ بِٱلصَّلَوٰةِ وَٱصۡطَبِرۡ عَلَيۡهَاۖ لَا نَسۡـَٔلُكَ رِزۡقٗاۖ نَّحۡنُ نَرۡزُقُكَۗ وَٱلۡعَٰقِبَةُ لِلتَّقۡوَىٰ ١٣٢\nMeaning: We do not ask you to provide provision for yourself and for them, and be distracted from prayer, rather, We will take care of your provision and theirs. When the Prophet (ﷺ) family faced some hardships, he would command them to pray. Al-Qurtubi: 14/165.\nIs being distracted from prayer by pursuing provision an excuse? What is your advice to one who is distracted from prayer by his job?\nwords\nالقُرُونِDisbelieving nations\nلَكَانَ لِزَامًاA punishment would have been an obligation due immediately\nآنَاءِTime periods\nمُتَرَبِّصٌWaiting\nالسَّوِيِّStraight"],[322,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nEnsure to say the morning Athkar before sunrise, and the evening Athkar before sunset, lest you become distracted.\nAsk a scholar about an issue of which you have no knowledge.\nReflect on one of the verses that you say in your Athkar today.\nguid\nYour reckoning is near, do you feel that?!\nThe one who pursues the truth demands a proof in order to be convinced, not to frustrate his opponent.\nBe keen on seeking knowledge, for a student of knowledge has a high rank in worldly life and the Hereafter.\nrefl\nٱقۡتَرَبَ لِلنَّاسِ حِسَابُهُمۡ وَهُمۡ فِي غَفۡلَةٖ مُّعۡرِضُونَ ١\nWhoever knew the nearness of the Hour (Day of Resurrection), his hopes would be curtailed, his soul would be content with repentance, and he would not incline toward this worldly life. To him, the past would seem as if it did not happen, every awaited event is near, thus, death is near. The death of a man is facing his Hour. The Hour is near, in comparison to what has passed of time, the time left of this worldly life is indeed less than what already gone. Al-Qurtubi: 14/171.\nAllah reminds us of the nearness of the Hour. Why? How does that affect the believer?\nلَاهِيَةٗ قُلُوبُهُمۡۗ\n(With their hearts distracted), heedless. These people, described in the Quran, would listen to it with absent minds and inattentive hearts. They would neither reflect on its wisdom, nor would they think about its arguments that Allah revealed against them. Al-Tabari: 18/410.\nWhat is the description of one who does not reflect on the Quran?\nفَسۡـَٔلُوٓاْ أَهۡلَ ٱلذِّكۡرِ إِن كُنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٧\nWe are only instructed to ask them because they are obliged to teach and answer questions about what they know. Al-Saadi: 519.\nWhat are the obligations of scholars and students of knowledge toward the community?\nفَسۡـَٔلُوٓاْ أَهۡلَ ٱلذِّكۡرِ إِن كُنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٧\nSince we are specifically instructed to ask those who have knowledge, it implies that it is not allowed to ask questions of those who are known to be ignorant and to have no knowledge, and it is prohibited for one who has no knowledge to give answers. Al-Saadi: 519.\nProof can only be established by asking someone with a specific trait. What is it?\nفَسۡـَٔلُوٓاْ أَهۡلَ ٱلذِّكۡرِ إِن كُنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٧\n(So ask): There is a consensus among scholars that this instruction is directed to the public Muslim community, and that they should follow their scholars. Al-Qurtubi: 14/179.\nWhat is the duty of a person who has no knowledge?\nلَقَدۡ أَنزَلۡنَآ إِلَيۡكُمۡ كِتَٰبٗا فِيهِ ذِكۡرُكُمۡۚ أَفَلَا تَعۡقِلُونَ ١٠\n(In which is your mention), your honor, pride, and lofty status if you pay heed to what it contains of true narrations, then believe in it, comply with what it enjoins and avoid what it forbids. Then you will rise in status and become significant. Al-Saadi: 519.\nWhen does this Book (the Quran) become a source of our honor, pride, and lofty status?\nلَقَدۡ أَنزَلۡنَآ إِلَيۡكُمۡ كِتَٰبٗا فِيهِ ذِكۡرُكُمۡۚ أَفَلَا تَعۡقِلُونَ ١٠\nThe word, (Book), is an indefinite form that indicates veneration of the Quran since it has two great attributes: A book of guidance, and being a sign and a miracle of the Messenger (ﷺ), which no one can produce the like of it, or come close to that. Ibn Ashur: 17/22.\nThe word: (Book) is in an indefinite form. Why?\nwords\nمُحدَثٍA new revelation\nوَأَسَرُّوا النَّجوَىThey concealed their private conversation\nأَضغَاثُ أَحلاَمٍA mixture of false dreams\nجَسَدًاBodies that are abnormal\nفِيهِ ذِكرُكُمIn which there is honor for you"],[323,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to make your place of residence and every provision He provides you a means to obey Him.\nIdentify, today, one of the righteous worshipers, and try to follow his example in some of his worships.\nIn the morning and evening, say, as many as ten times, \"None is worthy of worship but Allah alone, Who has no partner. To Him belongs all sovereignty and all praise, and He is Capable over all things.\"\nguid\nShirk, which is the highest level of transgression, must be denounced.\nReflect on the Allah's destruction of past and present nations.\nThe Quran and Sunnah have responses to all doubts that are raised about the religion, so pursue the knowledge of Sharia.\nrefl\nبَلۡ نَقۡذِفُ بِٱلۡحَقِّ عَلَى ٱلۡبَٰطِلِ فَيَدۡمَغُهُۥ فَإِذَا هُوَ زَاهِقٞۚ\nThis is general in meaning and applies to all religious matters. No supporter of falsehood presents a specious argument, basing it on reason or on a text that supports falsehood or rejects truth, but there is definitive evidence from Allah that is based on reason or texts that will defeat the false argument and suppress it. Thus, the falsehood thereof will become clear to everyone. Al-Saadi: 520.\nWhat is the best way to nullify the doubts of polytheists and those of corrupt minds?\nوَلَكُمُ ٱلۡوَيۡلُ مِمَّا تَصِفُونَ ١٨\n(And woe to you) O disbelievers (for what you falsely ascribe) to Allah what is unfitting such as a wife and a son. Al-Baghawi: 3/154.\nIn recent times, we have see some who ascribe to Allah, His Messenger (ﷺ), or Islam things that are extremely improper. In light of this verse, what is the punishment for that?\nوَمَنۡ عِندَهُۥ لَا يَسۡتَكۡبِرُونَ عَنۡ عِبَادَتِهِۦ وَلَا يَسۡتَحۡسِرُونَ ١٩\n(And those who are with Him) namely the angels, (are not too proud to worship Him, nor do they ever grow weary) that is, they never tire of worship, because their keenness is immense, their love is complete and their bodies are strong. Al-Saadi: 520-521.\nWhen does the servant become closer to Allah?\nأَمِ ٱتَّخَذُوٓاْ ءَالِهَةٗ مِّنَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ هُمۡ يُنشِرُونَ ٢١\nAllah mocks the polytheists and shows their weak minds by describing their gods as (from the earth), which means that they worshiped gods made of pieces of stone or wood that were collected from the ground. He alludes to the fact that such things do not deserve to be worshiped. Ibn Ashur: 17/37.\nThis verse mocks the polytheists. How?\nلَوۡ كَانَ فِيهِمَآ ءَالِهَةٌ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ لَفَسَدَتَاۚ فَسُبۡحَٰنَ ٱللَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَرۡشِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ ٢٢\nThis verse stipulates two things, first: The negation of multiple gods, and that God must be One. Second: This One God is none but Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/34.\nThis verse stipulates two things in proving the Oneness of Allah. Explain.\nلَا يُسۡـَٔلُ عَمَّا يَفۡعَلُ وَهُمۡ يُسۡـَٔلُونَ ٢٣\nNo one questions Allah about His decrees in His creation; rather, He questions them about their deeds since they are His servants. Al-Qurtubi: 14/189.\nThis verse indicates the obligation to submit to Sharia. Explain.\nبَلۡ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٱلۡحَقَّۖ فَهُم مُّعۡرِضُونَ ٢٤\nThe fact that they do not have any knowledge of the truth is not because it is hidden or unclear; rather it is because they turn away from it. Otherwise, if they paid the slightest attention to it, they would know truth from falsehood in a very clear way. Al-Saadi: 521.\nWhat is the reason that most people go astray?\nwords\nأَحَسُّواThey saw\nحَصِيدًاLike a harvest mowed down\nخَامِدِينَThey became lifeless\nفَيَدمَغُهُIt refutes and destroys it\nوَلاَ يَستَحسِرُونَThey never grow weary\nلاَ يَفتُرُونَThey never tire"],[324,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nHasten to write your will today.\nAsk Allah to make you fearful in awe of Him in private and in public.\nImagine if water is cut off from your town for a week, what will happen to the residents? Then, thank Allah for the blessing of water.\nguid\nFollow the example of the Prophets (p) in starting your preaching of others by establishing awareness about Allah in an endearing way.\nThe believer follows instructions only if they do not contradict Allah's commands.\nThe believer is constantly tested by either good and blessings or by evil and afflictions, so that Allah may reveal those who are grateful for the blessings, and those who bear patiently with afflictions.\nrefl\nوَقَالُواْ ٱتَّخَذَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ وَلَدٗاۗ سُبۡحَٰنَهُۥۚ بَلۡ عِبَادٞ مُّكۡرَمُونَ ٢٦\nSince taking a son is considered an imperfection of Allah, who is of necessary existence, therefore, after their statement, He says, (Exalted is He), exalting Himself above that.Taking a son originates from the need to fulfill a temporary shortage when missing a son. Ibn Ashur: 17/50.\nWhat is the wisdom behind mentioning exaltation after their statement?\nلَا يَسۡبِقُونَهُۥ بِٱلۡقَوۡلِ\nMeaning: They do not say anything that has to do with the affairs of His dominion until Allah speaks, because of their perfect etiquette and their awareness of the perfect nature of His wisdom and knowledge. Al-Saadi: 522.\nThe angels never precede Allah in words. Why?\nوَمَن يَقُلۡ مِنۡهُمۡ إِنِّيٓ إِلَٰهٞ مِّن دُونِهِۦ فَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِيهِ جَهَنَّمَۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٢٩\nWhat wrongdoing could be greater than that of an imperfect creature, who needs Allah in all ways, claiming to share with Allah the attributes of divinity and Lordship? Al-Saadi: 522.\nThere is no greater wrongdoing than for a creature to claim divinity. Why?\nوَمَا جَعَلۡنَا لِبَشَرٖ مِّن قَبۡلِكَ ٱلۡخُلۡدَۖ أَفَإِيْن مِّتَّ فَهُمُ ٱلۡخَٰلِدُونَ ٣٤\nThe reason for revealing this verse is that the disbelievers criticize the mortality of the Prophet (ﷺ). Moreover, it is said that they wished for his death in order to gloat over him, and this interpretation is more in line with the next verse. Ibn Juzay: 2/36.\nHow does the Quran respond to those who criticize the Prophet (ﷺ) for being a mortal human?\nكُلُّ نَفۡسٖ ذَآئِقَةُ ٱلۡمَوۡتِۗ\nThis verse highlights the falsehood of the view of those who say that Al-Khidr is still alive and that he is immortal in this world. This is a view for which there is no proof and it is contrary to the Sharia evidence. Al-Saadi: 523.\nSome people claim that Al-Khidr is immortal in this life. What do you think?\nكُلُّ نَفۡسٖ ذَآئِقَةُ ٱلۡمَوۡتِۗ وَنَبۡلُوكُم بِٱلشَّرِّ وَٱلۡخَيۡرِ فِتۡنَةٗۖ وَإِلَيۡنَا تُرۡجَعُونَ ٣٥\n(And We test you with evil and with good as a trial), We test you with poverty and richness, with health and sickness, and other things in this worldly life, so that your patience would show during affliction, and your gratitude would show during the blessing; or other than that may show up. Ibn Juzay: 2/36.\nWhat is the wisdom behind diversifying the test through evil and good?\nوَنَبۡلُوكُم بِٱلشَّرِّ وَٱلۡخَيۡرِ فِتۡنَةٗۖ وَإِلَيۡنَا تُرۡجَعُونَ ٣٥\nIbn Zayd said: \"It means: We test them with what they like and dislike; We test them to see their gratitude in what they like, and their patience in what they dislike.\" Al-Tabari: 18/440.\nHow is testing with good and evil carried out?\nwords\nرَتقًاJoined together\nفَفَتَقنَاهُمَاWe separated them\nرَوَاسِيَFirmly set mountains\nأَن تَمِيدَLest it should shift\nفِجَاجًا سُبُلًاBroad pathways\nمَحفُوظًاDoes no fall down, nor pierced by the devils\nفِي فَلَكٍ يَسبَحُونَEach is floating in a precise orbit"],[325,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nListen to a lecture given by a scholar to learn and become a successor, for part of reducing the land is the death of scholars.\nGive a talk or share a message in which you explain that whoever is steadfast in his faith will have the best outcome while those who ridicule them will be at a loss.\nPerform Al-Fajr prayer in congregation, then say your morning and evening Athkar, seeking Allah's protection.\nguid\nHaste is a basic nature of man, so whoever went along with it, will lose, but whoever strived to change his natural inclination and control himself to have patience, forbearance and graciousness, will attain the best outcome and become an example for others.\nThe enjoinment and adornments of worldly life is a cause for misguidance of most people.\nReflection on the affairs of destroyed nations is a cause for becoming nearer to Allah and avoiding sins and disobedience.\nrefl\nوَإِذَا رَءَاكَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِن يَتَّخِذُونَكَ إِلَّا هُزُوًا أَهَٰذَا ٱلَّذِي يَذۡكُرُ ءَالِهَتَكُمۡ وَهُم بِذِكۡرِ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ هُمۡ كَٰفِرُونَ ٣٦ خُلِقَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ مِنۡ عَجَلٖۚ سَأُوْرِيكُمۡ ءَايَٰتِي فَلَا تَسۡتَعۡجِلُونِ ٣٧\nThe reason why the haste of man is mentioned here is that when mention is made of those who mock the Messenger (ﷺ), the believers wanted to take revenge on them swiftly. Allah says, (Man is created of haste) because He gives respite to the transgressor until his time comes, and once He seizes him, He will never let him go. Ibn Kathir: 3/175.\nWhat is the wisdom behind mentioning haste after mentioning the mockers of the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nخُلِقَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ مِنۡ عَجَلٖۚ سَأُوْرِيكُمۡ ءَايَٰتِي فَلَا تَسۡتَعۡجِلُونِ ٣٧\nBe aware that there is no disparity between this verse (Man was created of haste) and (so do not ask Me to hasten them). One may say: How does Allah say that man is created of haste and predisposed to it, then He forbids him from acting based on his disposition? Because it is attainable for him. We say: Yes, man is predisposed to haste, but he can control himself to become patient, just as he is predisposed to loving desirable things, but he can control himself and keep it way. Al-Shanqiti: 4/152.\nHow do you reconcile the fact that haste is a man's nature, and yet he is commanded to do the opposite of his nature?\nلَوۡ يَعۡلَمُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ حِينَ لَا يَكُفُّونَ عَن وُجُوهِهِمُ ٱلنَّارَ وَلَا عَن ظُهُورِهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يُنصَرُونَ ٣٩\nAllah mentions the (faces) because the face is the most honored part of man, in addition to the fact that it has all the senses, and man does his utmost to defend his face. Then, Allah mentions the (backs) to indicate the spread of fire all over their bodies. Ibn Atiyah: 4/83.\nFaces and backs are singled out for mention in this verse. Why?\nقُلۡ مَن يَكۡلَؤُكُم بِٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ مِنَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِۚ بَلۡ هُمۡ عَن ذِكۡرِ رَبِّهِم مُّعۡرِضُونَ ٤٢\n(Say, \"Who can protect you\"), who guards you, which means: Say, there is no protector of you at night when you are asleep, and during the day when you are engaged in your affairs. Al-Qurtubi: 14/207-208.\nHave you felt Allah's protection over you at night and during the day?\nقُلۡ مَن يَكۡلَؤُكُم بِٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ مِنَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِۚ بَلۡ هُمۡ عَن ذِكۡرِ رَبِّهِم مُّعۡرِضُونَ ٤٢\nThe mention of (night) comes first because it is a time of fears. In darkness, the means for causing harm by humans, animals, and sickness in the body are easier. Ibn Ashur: 17/74.\nIn this verse, the mention of (night) precedes the mention of (day), why?\nبَلۡ مَتَّعۡنَا هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ وَءَابَآءَهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ طَالَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡعُمُرُۗ\nMeaning: We have extended for them and their fathers the enjoinment of this life, which was prolonged for them until they thought that it would never cease; they became deluded and turned away from reflecting on the signs of Allah, the Almighty. Al-Qurtubi: 14/209.\nWhen does the servant become deluded by the blessings of Allah upon him?\nبَلۡ مَتَّعۡنَا هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ وَءَابَآءَهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ طَالَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡعُمُرُۗ أَفَلَا يَرَوۡنَ أَنَّا نَأۡتِي ٱلۡأَرۡضَ نَنقُصُهَا مِنۡ أَطۡرَافِهَآۚ أَفَهُمُ ٱلۡغَٰلِبُونَ ٤٤\n(We have provided good things for these [disbelievers]), We have given them enjoyment with blessings and good health in worldly life, but they transgressed and forgot Allah's punishment. Ibn Juzay: 2/37.\nWhen do wealth and bliss become disastrous to the servant?\nwords\nفَتَبهَتُهُمIt stuns them\nفَحَاقَIt encompassed them\nيَكلَؤُكُمHe protects you, guards you\nيُصحَبُونَThey would be protected"],[326,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nRemind one of your relatives or collogues of a Quranic verse or a Prophetic Hadith.\nRecall someone whom you wronged in his property, honor or rights, and ask for his pardon before you become unable to do so.\nReflect on the story of Abraham (u), and extract two successful methods of dialogue or forbidding evil.\nguid\nLoving something to the extreme causes deafness that blocks everything from consideration except what one loves.\nThe one who uses proofs from the Quran and Sunnah in his preaching and admonishing is an effective and a convincing debater.\nFacing pains and difficulties in life is a reminder to you of Allah's punishment, and an incentive for you to repent and seek His forgiveness.\nrefl\nقُلۡ إِنَّمَآ أُنذِرُكُم بِٱلۡوَحۡيِۚ وَلَا يَسۡمَعُ ٱلصُّمُّ ٱلدُّعَآءَ إِذَا مَا يُنذَرُونَ ٤٥\nQatadah said: \"Contrary to the believer and faithful who hear the Quran, the disbeliever has become deaf to the Book of Allah; he does not hear, nor benefit , nor understand it.\" Al-Tabari: 18/450.\nWhat is the difference between a believer and a disbeliever toward the Book of Allah?\nوَلَا يَسۡمَعُ ٱلصُّمُّ ٱلدُّعَآءَ إِذَا مَا يُنذَرُونَ ٤٥\nMeaning: One who is deaf cannot hear any voice, for the faculty of hearing is absent in his case. Hearing is stipulated in addition to the voice, for the means of receiving the sound should be present. Likewise, the revelation causes the heart to spring to life (spiritual life), and makes one understand what Allah wants from us. But if the heart is not receptive to guidance, then relative to guidance and faith, it will be like the deaf person with regard to sounds and voices. Al-Saadi: 524.\nWhy are the disbelievers described as (deaf)? How does a person prepare himself to benefit from the Book of Allah, the Almighty?\nوَلَئِن مَّسَّتۡهُمۡ نَفۡحَةٞ مِّنۡ عَذَابِ رَبِّكَ لَيَقُولُنَّ يَٰوَيۡلَنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا ظَٰلِمِينَ ٤٦\nIt means that if the least torment touches them, (they would surely say, \"Woe to us! We were indeed wrongdoers\"), which means transgressors; thus, they admit to their guilt, but it will be of no benefit. Al-Qurtubi: 14/211.\nHow does man react when a whiff of Allah's torment touches him?\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَىٰ وَهَٰرُونَ ٱلۡفُرۡقَانَ وَضِيَآءٗ وَذِكۡرٗا لِّلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٤٨\nThe righteous are singled out for mention because they are the ones who benefit from that in terms of both knowledge and deeds. Al-Saadi: 525.\nWhy are the righteous singled out for mention?\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَىٰ وَهَٰرُونَ ٱلۡفُرۡقَانَ وَضِيَآءٗ وَذِكۡرٗا لِّلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٤٨ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخۡشَوۡنَ رَبَّهُم بِٱلۡغَيۡبِ\nMeaning: They fear Him when they are hiding away and no one sees them, so it is more apt when they are in the view of others that they refrain from that which is prohibited and do what is obligatory. Al-Saadi: 525.\nWhat is the wisdom behind linking fear of Allah with the unseen?\nوَهَٰذَا ذِكۡرٞ مُّبَارَكٌ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُۚ أَفَأَنتُمۡ لَهُۥ مُنكِرُونَ ٥٠\nDescribing the Quran as (blessed) includes all types of good because blessing means the increase of good. Thus, the Quran is full of good in terms of its eloquent style, and the ease with which it can be memorized and recited. Moreover, it is full of good because it contains useful categories of knowledge, wisdom, legislation, and beautiful sayings. That is why many nations were guided by it over time, and those who believed in it benefited from it. Ibn Ashur: 17/90.\nList the types of blessings of the Quran.\nوَتَٱللَّهِ لَأَكِيدَنَّ أَصۡنَٰمَكُم بَعۡدَ أَن تُوَلُّواْ مُدۡبِرِينَ ٥٧\nAbraham (u) informed them that he would not be sufficed with verbal protesting, but would go further to smashing their idols, which is an indication of his trust in Allah's help and his firm stand in the face of harm for the sake of the religion. Al-Qurtubi: 14/216-217.\nExplain the level to which Abraham's (u) trust in Allah has reached.\nwords\nأُنذِرُكُمI warn you\nنَفحَةٌA slight touch\nمِثقَالَ حَبَّةٍThe weight of an atom\nفَطَرَهُنَّHe created them\nلأَكِيدَنI will plot, break\nمُدبِرِينَYou are gone away"],[327,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nRead a book on the skills of dialogue, convincing, winning arguments, and learn from the dialogues in the Quran and Sunnah.\nAsk Allah to grant you righteous offspring.\nBecome closer to Allah by performing an act of obedience to Him, so that He may save you at times of hardship.\nguid\nConfuting an opponent out of his own mouth is the most effective form of rebuttal.\nGuidance is not attained through reason or status of a person, rather, it is a blessing from Allah, the Almighty.\nObstinacy deprives one of the good of worldly life and the Hereafter.\nrefl\nفَجَعَلَهُمۡ جُذَٰذًا إِلَّا كَبِيرٗا لَّهُمۡ\nReflect on this prudent measure: Everything that is disdained by Allah should not be respected except when it is attributed to those who honor it. When the Prophet (ﷺ) used to write to the polytheist kings, he said: \"To the great of Persia\", \"To the great of Byzantine,\" but he did not say, \"To the great.\" Here, Allah says, (except a big one for them [polytheists]), and did not say, \"a big one of their idols.\" Therefore, it is prudent to safeguard against respecting that which Allah disdains. Al-Saadi: 526.\nAllah says, (except a big one for them [polytheists]), why?\nفَسۡـَٔلُوهُمۡ إِن كَانُواْ يَنطِقُونَ ٦٣\nHe aimed to let them admit of their own volition that these idols could not speak, and that this big idol could not do such a thing because it was inanimate. Ibn Kathir: 3/178.\nWhat was the aim of Abraham (u) behind asking this question?\nثُمَّ نُكِسُواْ عَلَىٰ رُءُوسِهِمۡ لَقَدۡ عَلِمۡتَ مَا هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ يَنطِقُونَ ٦٥\n(Then they reversed themselves), a metaphor is used in the Arabic text: \"On their heads,\" to indicate the recanting of their initial acceptance of the truth, and reverting to falsehood and obstinacy. They said, (You have already known that these do not speak), why are you telling us to ask them? Thus, they admitted that these idols do not speak, however, they continued to worship them, which showed the ultimate misguidance, stubbornness and obstinacy in their quarreling. Ibn Juzay: 2/39.\nWhat is the habit of the people of falsehood when the truth becomes apparent to them?\nقَالُواْ حَرِّقُوهُ وَٱنصُرُوٓاْ ءَالِهَتَكُمۡ إِن كُنتُمۡ فَٰعِلِينَ ٦٨\nWhen their arguments were refuted and their incapability became clear, when truth was made manifest and falsehood was defeated, they resorted to using their power and strength, and said: (Burn him and support your gods - if you are to act). Ibn Kathir: 3/179.\nThose who are unable to prove their argument resort to a different way. What is it?\nقُلۡنَا يَٰنَارُ كُونِي بَرۡدٗا وَسَلَٰمًا عَلَىٰٓ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ ٦٩\nAbu Al-'Aliyah said: \"Had Allah not said, (safe), its coolness would be more harmful to him than its heat, and had He not said, (for Abraham), its coolness would have lasted forever.\" Al-Shanqiti: 4/163.\nAllah commanded to the fire to be (safe for Abraham). Why?\nوَنَجَّيۡنَٰهُ وَلُوطًا إِلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ ٱلَّتِي بَٰرَكۡنَا فِيهَا لِلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٧١\nAbraham (u) migrated from Iraq to the Levant, where its blessing is in its fertility and the numerous Prophets who dwelled in it. Ibn Juzay: 2/40.\nWhat is the blessing of the Levant?\nوَوَهَبۡنَا لَهُۥٓ إِسۡحَٰقَ وَيَعۡقُوبَ نَافِلَةٗۖ وَكُلّٗا جَعَلۡنَا صَٰلِحِينَ ٧٢\n(And We gave him Isaac and Jacob in addition), He asked for a son (Isaac) and was given Jacob in addition, without asking. Abraham (u) said, (My Lord, grant me righteous offspring) [37:100]. In Arabic, a grand child is called \"Nafilah\", which means an addition. Al-Qurtubi: 14/230.\nScholars say that if a servant is truthful to Allah, He will give him more than he hopes for. How can you infer that from this verse?\nwords\nجُذَاذًاSmall pieces\nعَلَى أَعيُنِ النَّاسِBefore the eyes of the people\nنُكِسُوا عَلَى رُؤُوسِهِمThey returned to their obstinacy\nأُفٍّ لَكُمFie upon you\nنَافِلَةًIn addition to what he asked"],[328,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nConsole an afflicted person, give charity for the sake of Allah, or fast for a day voluntarily for the sake of Allah.\nSay, \"O Allah, the teacher of Abraham, teach me; the giver of understanding to Solomon, give me understanding.\"\nJoin a skills development course to acquire a useful skill.\nguid\nCalling others to Allah is a virtuous task that is carried out by honorable people.\nWhen wickedness spreads in a society, its doom is inevitable.\nWhen affliction strikes, call out to Allah, as there is no one who can give relief except Him.\nrefl\nوَجَعَلۡنَٰهُمۡ أَئِمَّةٗ يَهۡدُونَ بِأَمۡرِنَا\nThis is one of the greatest blessings that Allah may bestow upon His servant, by making him a leader by means of whom people are guided and whom many people follow. Al-Saadi: 527.\nAllah made Abraham (u) and his descendants leaders of guidance. What is a useful lesson in that? What blessing does a person who memorizes the Quran and the student of Islamic knowledge feel when they read this verse?\nوَأَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَيۡهِمۡ فِعۡلَ ٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِ وَإِقَامَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ وَإِيتَآءَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةِۖ\n(This includes all good deeds with respect to duties toward Allah and people. (Establish prayer and give zakah), this comes under the category of mentioning specific deeds after speaking in general terms due to the noble status and virtue of these two acts of worship. Whoever performs them properly, his religious commitment will be sound, but whoever neglects them will be more neglectful of other matters. Moreover, prayer is the best of the deeds that are due to Allah, and zakah is the best of the deeds that involve kindness toward His creation. Al-Saadi: 527.\nAllah singles the prayer and zakah for mention, even though they are included in righteous deeds. Why?\nوَدَاوُۥدَ وَسُلَيۡمَٰنَ إِذۡ يَحۡكُمَانِ فِي ٱلۡحَرۡثِ إِذۡ نَفَشَتۡ فِيهِ غَنَمُ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ وَكُنَّا لِحُكۡمِهِمۡ شَٰهِدِينَ ٧٨ فَفَهَّمۡنَٰهَا سُلَيۡمَٰنَۚ وَكُلًّا ءَاتَيۡنَا حُكۡمٗا وَعِلۡمٗاۚ\n(And We gave understanding of it to Solomon), We helped him to understand this case and reach the right verdict. This does not mean that Allah did not enable David to reach the right verdict in other cases. Hence, He pointed this out, as He says: (And to each of them), namely David and Solomon (We gave judgement and knowledge). This indicates that a judge may reach the right conclusion or he may get it wrong; he is not to be blamed if he makes a mistake so long as he did his best. Al-Saadi: 528.\nWhen is a ruler, a judge, a teacher, or a parent not blamed for a mistake?\nوَدَاوُۥدَ وَسُلَيۡمَٰنَ إِذۡ يَحۡكُمَانِ فِي ٱلۡحَرۡثِ إِذۡ نَفَشَتۡ فِيهِ غَنَمُ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ وَكُنَّا لِحُكۡمِهِمۡ شَٰهِدِينَ ٧٨ فَفَهَّمۡنَٰهَا سُلَيۡمَٰنَۚ وَكُلًّا ءَاتَيۡنَا حُكۡمٗا وَعِلۡمٗاۚ\nAlhasan said: \"If it was not for this verse, you would have seen all judges doomed, but Allah praised Solomon for being correct, and excused David for doing his best.\" Al-Qurtubi: 14/237.\nDescribe Allah's mercy toward scholars and judges in light of this verse.\nوَسَخَّرۡنَا مَعَ دَاوُۥدَ ٱلۡجِبَالَ يُسَبِّحۡنَ وَٱلطَّيۡرَۚ\nThat is because he was one of the most devoted of worshipers and one of those who remembered Allah the most, glorifying and praising Him. Al-Saadi: 528.\nAllah subjected the mountains and birds, along with David, to exalt Him. Why?\nوَسَخَّرۡنَا مَعَ دَاوُۥدَ ٱلۡجِبَالَ يُسَبِّحۡنَ وَٱلطَّيۡرَۚ وَكُنَّا فَٰعِلِينَ ٧٩\nIt is apparent that saying, (And We were doing that) is a confirmation of this verse: (And We subjected the mountains to exalt [Us], along with David and [also] the birds). The reason for this confirmation is that subjecting the mountains and their exaltation of Allah is a supernatural event, which is prone to denial by ignorant disbelievers. Al-Shanqiti: 4/232.\nThe verse ends with: (And We were doing that), why?\nوَعَلَّمۡنَٰهُ صَنۡعَةَ لَبُوسٖ لَّكُمۡ لِتُحۡصِنَكُم مِّنۢ بَأۡسِكُمۡۖ فَهَلۡ أَنتُمۡ شَٰكِرُونَ ٨٠\nThe servant's gratitude toward his Lord: Using His blessings to obey Him. The Lord’s appreciation toward his servant: Giving him a great reward for his small deed. Al-Shanqiti: 4/234.\nWhen is a servant described as (grateful)? How does Allah appreciate his servant?\nwords\nقَومَ سَوءٍPeople of evil, corruption\nنَفَشَتOverran it at night\nصَنعَةَ لَبُوسٍFashioning of coats of armor\nلِتُحصِنَكُمTo protect you\nبَأسِكُمYour battle\nعَاصِفَة[The wind] blowing forcefully"],[329,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nTell a story from the Quran about Prophets’ biographies to your siblings or children, explaining its useful lessons and valuable insights.\nRecall a sin after which a hardship struck, and say: [There is no deity except You; exalted are You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers].\nHasten to the five daily prayers right after the call (Athan).\nguid\nWhen in distress, do not hesitate to raise your hands, supplicating Allah, and saying:\nWhen facing extreme difficulties and hardships, return to the stories of Job, Joseph, or Muhammad (p), for they have consolations.\nEnduring hardships patiently has a high rank with Allah, and so does showing gratitude for His blessings.\nrefl\nوَأَيُّوبَ إِذۡ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُۥٓ أَنِّي مَسَّنِيَ ٱلضُّرُّ وَأَنتَ أَرۡحَمُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ٨٣ فَٱسۡتَجَبۡنَا لَهُۥ فَكَشَفۡنَا مَا بِهِۦ مِن ضُرّٖۖ وَءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ أَهۡلَهُۥ وَمِثۡلَهُم مَّعَهُمۡ رَحۡمَةٗ مِّنۡ عِندِنَا وَذِكۡرَىٰ لِلۡعَٰبِدِينَ ٨٤\n(And as a reminder for the worshipers [of Allah]), We made him an example, lest those who are beset by trial think that We do that to them because We do not care for them. Moreover, they may take him as an example of patience in accepting the decrees of Allah and bearing the trials with which He tests His servants as He wills. Ibn Kathir: 3/185.\nJob's story is a reminder for the worshipers of Allah. Why?\nرَحۡمَةٗ مِّنۡ عِندِنَا وَذِكۡرَىٰ لِلۡعَٰبِدِينَ ٨٤\nMeaning: We tested him to multiply his rewards. (And as a reminder for the worshipers [of Allah]), a reminder for the servants, because when they remember Job's (u) affliction, his patience and perseverance -while he was the best among the people of his time- they accustom themselves to endure the hardships of life with patience, just like Job (u) did. This alerts them to the importance of a continuing the worship and enduring harm with patience. Al-Qurtubi: 14/263.\nWhat is the wisdom behind Allah's mention of His testing of Job (u)?\nوَأَدۡخَلۡنَٰهُمۡ فِي رَحۡمَتِنَآۖ إِنَّهُم مِّنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ٨٦\nAllah, also, describes them as righteous, which includes righteousness of the heart, by knowing and loving Allah, and turning to Him at all times; righteousness of the tongue, by keeping it moist with the remembrance of Allah; and physical righteousness, by keeping their physical faculties busy with acts of obedience to Allah and restraining them from sin. Al-Saadi: 529.\nWhen is a person described as righteous?\nوَذَا ٱلنُّونِ إِذ ذَّهَبَ مُغَٰضِبٗا فَظَنَّ أَن لَّن نَّقۡدِرَ عَلَيۡهِ فَنَادَىٰ فِي ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ أَن لَّآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنتَ سُبۡحَٰنَكَ إِنِّي كُنتُ مِنَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٨٧\n(And he called out within the darknesses), the darknesses of the night, the sea and the whale's belly. Ibn Juzay: 2/43.\nWhat were the darknesses in which Prophet Jonah was? In light of this verse, explain briefly the effect of Allah's remembrance in relieving the affliction.\nلَّآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنتَ سُبۡحَٰنَكَ إِنِّي كُنتُ مِنَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٨٧\nThus, Prophet Jonah (u) affirmed the perfect divinity of Allah (there is no deity except You), declaring Him to be above any shortcomings, defects, or faults (exalted are You), and he acknowledged his own wrongdoing and transgression (indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers). Al-Saadi: 529.\nThis supplication includes three things for which Prophet Jonah (u) deserved to be saved from the whale's belly. What are they?\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ نُۨجِي ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٨٨\nMeaning: When they are in difficulty and they call upon Us and repent to Us, especially if they call upon Us with these words at the time of distress. Ibn Kathir: 3/187.\nInferring from this verse, what is an ideal way to be saved during times of hardships?\nفَٱسۡتَجَبۡنَا لَهُۥ وَوَهَبۡنَا لَهُۥ يَحۡيَىٰ وَأَصۡلَحۡنَا لَهُۥ زَوۡجَهُۥٓۚ\n(And amended for him his wife), after she was a barren, and her womb had been unable to bear children, Allah healed her and made her womb able to bear a child for the sake of His Prophet Zachariah (u). This is one of the benefits of having good and righteous companions, for those who keep company with them will be blessed. Thus, John (u) was born to his parents. Al-Saadi: 530.\nIn light of this verse, how do you infer the blessing of the righteous companion?\nwords\nيَغُوصُونَ لَهُThey dive in the seas to bring him pearls\nنَقدِرَ عَلَيهِWe would not take him to task\nخَيرُ الوَارِثِينَThe Best of Inheritors\nرَغَبًا وَرَهَبًاIn hope for reward, and fear of punishment"],[330,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from the trial of Gog and Magog.\nVisit a cemetery, lest you be heedless of the Hereafter.\nAsk Allah to be among those whom He has decreed the finest reward, and those who will be far away from Hellfire.\nguid\nPurity, self-respect and guarding own chastity are all great virtues.\nThe sincere belief in the Oneness of Allah is the foundation for uniting Muslim nation.\nThe belief [in Allah] is a pre-condition for accepting righteous deeds.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّتِيٓ أَحۡصَنَتۡ فَرۡجَهَا فَنَفَخۡنَا فِيهَا مِن رُّوحِنَا وَجَعَلۡنَٰهَا وَٱبۡنَهَآ ءَايَةٗ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٩١\nHere, Allah mentions the story of Mary and her son Jesus (q) with the story of Zachariah and his son John (u). He mentions the story of Zachariah first, followed by the story of Mary, because one is connected to the other. The former is the story of a child being born to an old man of advanced years, to an old woman who had been barren and had never given birth when she was younger. Then, Allah mentions the story of Mary, which is even more wondrous, for in this case a child was born to a female without (the involvement of) a male. These stories appear in Surat Al-Imran, Surat Maryam, and here. Ibn Kathir: 3/189.\nThe story of Mary and Jesus is often mentioned with the story of Zachariah and John. Why?\nإِنَّ هَٰذِهِۦٓ أُمَّتُكُمۡ أُمَّةٗ وَٰحِدَةٗ وَأَنَا۠ رَبُّكُمۡ فَٱعۡبُدُونِ ٩٢\nMeaning: This religion is the religion of all the Messengers mentioned. They are your leaders whose example you follow. They all follow one religion and one path, and they all worship one Lord. Hence Allah says: (And I am your Lord). Al-Saadi: 530.\nHow do all the Messengers and their followers belong to the same religion?\nإِنَّ هَٰذِهِۦٓ أُمَّتُكُمۡ أُمَّةٗ وَٰحِدَةٗ وَأَنَا۠ رَبُّكُمۡ فَٱعۡبُدُونِ ٩٢ وَتَقَطَّعُوٓاْ أَمۡرَهُم بَيۡنَهُمۡۖ كُلٌّ إِلَيۡنَا رَٰجِعُونَ ٩٣\nMeaning: Your religion is one religion as long as you all believed in the Oneness of Allah, but if you differ among yourselves and become separated, then those who reject the truth are not part of the true religion. Al-Qurtubi: 14/283.\nExplain the importance of coming together to the truth and refraining from dispute.\nإِنَّ هَٰذِهِۦٓ أُمَّتُكُمۡ أُمَّةٗ وَٰحِدَةٗ وَأَنَا۠ رَبُّكُمۡ فَٱعۡبُدُونِ ٩٢\nThe meaning of one religion is the belief in the Oneness of Allah, who has no other god besides Him. This is the nature of divine Sharia, which is in contrast to the religions of polytheism that have multiple religions due to multiple gods, where for each god there are many worship acts and followers. However, they all come under the description of shirk (polytheism). Ibn Ashur: 17/141.\nThe Oneness of Allah unites the people while polytheism divides them. Explain.\nوَٱقۡتَرَبَ ٱلۡوَعۡدُ ٱلۡحَقُّ فَإِذَا هِيَ شَٰخِصَةٌ أَبۡصَٰرُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ\nOn that day, you will see the eyes of the disbelievers staring in horror because of the intensity of fear, great terror, and immense turmoil, and because of what they know of their offences and sins. They will pray against themselves and call for doom, in regret and sorrow for what has passed. Al-Saadi: 531.\nThe disbelievers' eyes will be staring in horror on the Day of Resurrection. Why?\nإِنَّكُمۡ وَمَا تَعۡبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ حَصَبُ جَهَنَّمَ أَنتُمۡ لَهَا وَٰرِدُونَ ٩٨\nJesus (u) and Ezra and other righteous people are worshiped besides Allah, however, they abhorred being worshiped and obeyed by others in clear disobedience to Allah. Allah decreed for them the finest reward because He says, (But those for whom We have decreed the finest reward, they will be far away from it), so they will be far away from Hellfire. Ibn Taimyah: 4/393.\nJesus (u), Alhusain (t), and Al-Jeelani are worshiped besides Allah, so, will they be included in this verse? Why?\nإِنَّكُمۡ وَمَا تَعۡبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ حَصَبُ جَهَنَّمَ أَنتُمۡ لَهَا وَٰرِدُونَ ٩٨\nThe wisdom behind the admission of the idols into Hellfire, even though they are inanimate and cannot think, and there is no sin on their part, is to highlight the lies of those who took them as gods, and so as to increase their punishment. Al-Saadi: 531.\nWhat is the wisdom behind the admission of the idols to Hellfire?\nwords\nوَتَقَطَّعُوا أَمرَهُمThey differed with their Messengers and became divided\nفَلاَ كُفرَانَ لِسَعيِهِThere will be no denial for his efforts\nحَدَبٍMound, elevation\nيَنسِلُونَThey swarm swiftly\nشَاخِصَةٌFixedly staring eyes, not blinking\nحَصَبُ جَهَنَّمَFuel for Hellfire"],[331,"§Al-Anbiya\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to establish His righteous servants in the land.\nShare a message in which you describe the aspects of the Prophet's (ﷺ) mercy toward the creation.\nAsk for Allah's help in everything you do.\nguid\nSubmission to Allah and righteousness are causes for inheriting the land.\nHold fast to this Quran, memorize it, and learn its meanings, as it has a sufficient and a healing message to anyone who does that.\nMaintaining various types of acts of worship is a cause for success in understanding and adhering to the Holy Quran.\nrefl\nلَا يَحۡزُنُهُمُ ٱلۡفَزَعُ ٱلۡأَكۡبَرُ\nThe greatest terror is the immense turmoil of the Day of Judgment and Resurrection. Alhasan said: \"It is the time when people will be commanded to Hellfire.\" Ibn Jurayj , Saeed bin Jubair, and Al-Dhahhak said: \"It is the time when Hellfire will be slammed shut on its dwellers, and death will be slaughtered between Paradise and Hellfire.\" Al-Qurtubi: 14/295.\nThe believers will not be grieved by the greatest terror in the Hereafter. Why?\nيَوۡمَ نَطۡوِي ٱلسَّمَآءَ كَطَيِّ ٱلسِّجِلِّ لِلۡكُتُبِۚ كَمَا بَدَأۡنَآ أَوَّلَ خَلۡقٖ نُّعِيدُهُۥۚ وَعۡدًا عَلَيۡنَآۚ إِنَّا كُنَّا فَٰعِلِينَ ١٠٤\nIn Sahih Muslim, Ibn Abbas (k) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up to give an admonition and said: \"O people, you will be gathered to Allah, bare-footed, naked and uncircumcised.\" Then he recited this verse: (Just as We originated the first creation, so We will bring it back. That is Our binding promise, which We will surely do). Ibn Ashur: 17/161.\nIn light of this verse, explain how the Prophet (ﷺ) used to admonish people.\nوَلَقَدۡ كَتَبۡنَا فِي ٱلزَّبُورِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ٱلذِّكۡرِ أَنَّ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ يَرِثُهَا عِبَادِيَ ٱلصَّٰلِحُونَ ١٠٥\n(The land), in general, means the lands of the east and west. It is also said: The holy land. Moreover, it is said: The land of Paradise, but the first interpretation is more likely. (Righteous servants) are the Muslim nation of Muhammad (ﷺ), for they are praised in this verse. This is also informing about unseen events that later became true when Muslims conquered the east and west of the land. Ibn Juzay: 2/46.\nWhat are the traits of those whom Allah promised to make them inherit the land?\nوَلَقَدۡ كَتَبۡنَا فِي ٱلزَّبُورِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ٱلذِّكۡرِ أَنَّ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ يَرِثُهَا عِبَادِيَ ٱلصَّٰلِحُونَ ١٠٥\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"It means the lands of the disbelievers that will be conquered by Muslims, and this is a decree of Allah to empower the religion of Islam and Muslims.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/196\nThis verse contains a glad tidings to the righteous people. What is it?\nوَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَٰكَ إِلَّا رَحۡمَةٗ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٠٧\nIn general, the meaning is: Allah had mercy on the worlds by sending our master, Muhammad (ﷺ), because he came with the great joy and salvation from eternal misery. At his hands, his followers attained much good in this life and in the Hereafter; he taught them after they were ignorant, and guided them after being strayed. Ibn Juzay: 2/46.\nHow did the Prophet (ﷺ) become a given mercy?\nوَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَٰكَ إِلَّا رَحۡمَةٗ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٠٧\nIf it is said: He is a mercy to the worlds, but the disbelievers did not receive that mercy? The answer can be in two ways: First: The disbelievers would have received mercy had they believed in him, but they were the ones who abandoned the mercy after they were exposed to it. Second: They received mercy because of him since they were not punished swiftly like the previous disbelievers who were destroyed by the deluge, the great cry, and akin to it. Ibn Juzay: 2/46.\nWhat is the answer to the saying that (a mercy to the worlds) is general, yet the disbelievers did not receive the mercy?\nوَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَٰكَ إِلَّا رَحۡمَةٗ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٠٧\n(And We have not sent you [O Prophet] except as a mercy to the worlds), Ibn Abbas (k) said: \"The mercy has been fulfilled in this life and in the Hereafter for those who believed in him; for those who did not believe in him, they were spared the punishment which struck the ones before them.\" Al-Tabari: 18/552.\nHow did our Prophet (ﷺ) become a mercy to the believers and disbelievers?\nwords\nحَسِيسَهَاThe sound of its flames and burning bodies\nالفَزَعُ الأَكبَرThe greatest terror of the Day of Resurrection\nكَطَيِّ السِّجِلِّ لِلكُتُبRolled up like a scroll of records\nالزَّبُورِThe Revealed Scriptures\nالذِّكرThe Preserved Tablet\nآذَنتُكُمI have proclaimed the message to you\nعَلَى سَوَاءٍYou and I are equally informed about this"],[332,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nAsk Allah for safety on the Day of terror, then say, \"O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity and self-sufficiency.\"\nGive a talk, or share a message in which you show the risk of arguing about the religion without proper knowledge.\nAsk refuge with Allah from reaching decrepit old age.\nguid\nAffirming the belief in resurrection and recompense by stating their immense turmoil.\nSpeaking about Sharia of Allah without knowledge from the divine revelation or a Prophetic authentic Hadith is strictly prohibited.\nThe alliance with the devils and their followers will lead one to go astray and enter Hellfire.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ ٱتَّقُواْ رَبَّكُمۡۚ\nHere, Allah addresses all people, telling them to fear their Lord Who has bestowed upon them all sorts of blessings, both visible and hidden. Therefore, they should fear Him and refrain from ascription of partners to Him, evildoing and sin; and they should comply with His commands as much as possible. Al-Saadi: 532.\nAmong Allah's Names and Attributes, the (Lord) is singled out for mention here. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ ٱتَّقُواْ رَبَّكُمۡۚ إِنَّ زَلۡزَلَةَ ٱلسَّاعَةِ شَيۡءٌ عَظِيمٞ ١ يَوۡمَ تَرَوۡنَهَا تَذۡهَلُ كُلُّ مُرۡضِعَةٍ عَمَّآ أَرۡضَعَتۡ وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذَاتِ حَمۡلٍ حَمۡلَهَا وَتَرَى ٱلنَّاسَ سُكَٰرَىٰ وَمَا هُم بِسُكَٰرَىٰ وَلَٰكِنَّ عَذَابَ ٱللَّهِ شَدِيدٞ ٢\nThe benefit of mentioning the immense turmoil of that Day is to urge people to prepare for it, and be ready through doing righteous deeds. Al-Qurtubi: 14/311.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning the immense turmoil of the Day of Resurrection?\nيَوۡمَ تَرَوۡنَهَا تَذۡهَلُ كُلُّ مُرۡضِعَةٍ عَمَّآ أَرۡضَعَتۡ\nA nursing mother will be distracted from her child even though she naturally has deep love for him, especially at this stage at which the infant cannot survive without her. Al-Saadi: 533.\nWhy is the nursing mother singled out for mention here?\nيَوۡمَ تَرَوۡنَهَا تَذۡهَلُ كُلُّ مُرۡضِعَةٍ عَمَّآ أَرۡضَعَتۡ\nIn Arabic, the word used for \"nursing mother\" has two variations: A general descriptive term, and a present continuous term. The one used in this verse is the present continuous term in order to reflect the intensity of the distraction where the nursing mother will remove her child from her breast while he is still sucking and will let go of him at once. Ibn Juzay: 2/48.\nThe \"nursing mother\" is described eloquently. How?\nوَتَرَى ٱلنَّاسَ سُكَٰرَىٰ وَمَا هُم بِسُكَٰرَىٰ وَلَٰكِنَّ عَذَابَ ٱللَّهِ شَدِيدٞ ٢\nThey are described as intoxicated due to the immense distress they will be in. Ibn Juzay: 2/49.\nThey are described as intoxicated but they are not. Why?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يُجَٰدِلُ فِي ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖ وَيَتَّبِعُ كُلَّ شَيۡطَٰنٖ مَّرِيدٖ ٣\nIn his interpretation of the Quran, Fakhr Al-Din Al-Razi said: \"This verse permits fair arguing that is based on knowledge because, in this verse, only arguing without knowledge is prohibited, which proves that when proper knowledge is present, then arguing is allowed. Pointless arguing is what is meant by this verse: (They only mentioned him to you for the sake of argument) [43:58]. Fair arguing is meant by this verse: (And argue with them in a way that is best) [16:125].\" Al-Shanqiti: 4/263.\nThere are two types of arguing, what are they? Which one is permitted?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يُجَٰدِلُ فِي ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖ وَيَتَّبِعُ كُلَّ شَيۡطَٰنٖ مَّرِيدٖ ٣\nThis is the case of one who went astray by following one who misled him without details. He argues without knowledge and follows every rebellious devil, where it has been decreed that whoever takes him as an ally, he will misguide him and lead him to the punishment of the Blazing Fire. Moreover, this is the case of the followers of misguiding leaders among the people of the Scripture and those who have religious innovation, for they dispute about Allah without knowledge, and follow those who misguide them from among men and jinn devils. Ibn Taimyah: 4/401.\nExplain the risk of following misguiding leaders.\nwords\nتَذهَلُShe will be distracted\nمَرِيدٍA rebellious\nعَلَقَةٍA clinging clot\nمُضغَةٍA lump of flesh as big as a bite size\nمُخَلَّقَةٍFormed, completed"]])